{
  "_about": [
    "The WhatsApp message templates our code sends, as they must exist in OUR account",
    "(chapter அ, 1438047108420416). scripts/whatsapp-create-templates.py creates any",
    "that are missing. Wording was copied on 2026-10-10 from the Wamafy-era account;",
    "see docs/WHATSAPP-TEMPLATE-PACK-2026-10-10.md.",
    "",
    "RULES THE CODE DEPENDS ON",
    "1. Every template is language 'en'. The senders pass one language for all of them.",
    "2. Names must match what the edge functions send (cloudTemplate / template: ...).",
    "3. EVERY button is dynamic: https://chaptera.in/invite{{1}}. The code supplies the",
    "   tail (?phone=...&name=...&wa=<tap code>.<button>), one value per button. That",
    "   includes invitation_with_contact, whose buttons were fixed links on Wamafy and",
    "   AiSensy: here they are dynamic so the invite can carry a tap code too.",
    "4. Body {{n}} order must match the order the code passes its values in."
  ],
